/// known-gap: interp runs the class action but its field writes do not stick
/// Objects a judge arm passes go by reference, as in an ordinary call:
/// `strike(target, target, self)` changes one dummy twice, and reads through
/// `me` the change it made through `self`.
<>Dummy |
    ~hp: 10
xx
<>Fighter |
    ~want: 1
    ~seen: 5
    pick_one | decision against Dummy by [
        target >> hp
    ]
    judge using pick_one
        >= .5: strike(target, target, self)
        else: strike(target, target, self)
    end
    act strike(a, b, me)
        a >> hp |= a >> hp - 1
        b >> hp |= b >> hp - 1
        self >> want |= 0
        self >> seen |= me >> want
    end
xx
d <> Dummy | hp: 10
f <> Fighter | want: 1
tick()
say(d >> hp)
say(f >> seen)
